Input: {"question": "Which administrative body is twinned with Evansville?", "original_source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 0, "end": 106, "text": "**HEADLINE:** Transatlantic Ties: Osnabrück and Evansville Celebrate Decades-Long Sister City Relationship"}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 108, "end": 328, "text": "In a testament to the power of international cooperation and cultural exchange, the German city of Osnabrück and Evansville, Indiana, have been twinned for decades, fostering a strong bond between the two municipalities."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 329, "end": 523, "text": "According to official records, the sister city partnership between Osnabrück and Evansville was established in 1962, making it one of the longest-standing relationships of its kind in the world."}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 524, "end": 677, "text": "This unique connection has facilitated the exchange of ideas, cultures, and best practices between the two cities, enriching the lives of their citizens."}, "D1S5": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 678, "end": 775, "text": "\"We are proud to have Evansville as our sister city,\" said Wolfgang Griesert, Mayor of Osnabrück."}, "D1S6": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 776, "end": 965, "text": "\"Our partnership has led to numerous collaborations in fields such as education, business, and tourism, and we look forward to continuing this fruitful relationship for many years to come.\""}, "D1S7": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 966, "end": 1028, "text": "The partnership has yielded tangible benefits for both cities."}, "D1S8": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1029, "end": 1221, "text": "For instance, Evansville's University of Southern Indiana has a strong exchange program with Osnabrück University, allowing students to study abroad and gain valuable international experience."}, "D1S9": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1222, "end": 1366, "text": "Additionally, several businesses in Evansville have established ties with Osnabrück-based companies, promoting economic growth and job creation."}, "D1S10": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1367, "end": 1467, "text": "\"Osnabrück has been an invaluable partner for Evansville,\" said Lloyd Winnecke, Mayor of Evansville."}, "D1S11": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1468, "end": 1627, "text": "\"Our sister city relationship has opened doors to new opportunities, and we are grateful for the friendship and cooperation that has developed over the years.\""}, "D1S12": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1628, "end": 1911, "text": "Data from the Sister Cities International organization, a non-profit that facilitates international partnerships, reveals that Osnabrück and Evansville have engaged in numerous joint projects, including cultural festivals, educational exchanges, and economic development initiatives."}, "D1S13": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1912, "end": 2035, "text": "In 2019, a delegation from Evansville visited Osnabrück to celebrate the 57th anniversary of their sister city partnership."}, "D1S14": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2036, "end": 2172, "text": "The visit included a ceremony at Osnabrück's City Hall, where officials from both cities reaffirmed their commitment to the partnership."}, "D1S15": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2173, "end": 2353, "text": "As the world becomes increasingly interconnected, the bond between Osnabrück and Evansville serves as a shining example of the benefits of international cooperation and friendship."}, "D1S16": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2354, "end": 2550, "text": "As Mayor Griesert noted, \"Our sister city relationship is a testament to the power of people-to-people diplomacy, and we look forward to many more years of collaboration and mutual understanding.\""}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 0, "end": 31, "text": "Rosh HaAyin-Evansville Twinning"}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 33, "end": 216, "text": "The Rosh HaAyin-Evansville twinning is a sister city relationship between Rosh HaAyin, a city in Israel, and Evansville, the county seat of Vanderburgh County, Indiana, United States."}, "D2S3": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 217, "end": 354, "text": "This partnership was established in 2003, with the aim of promoting cultural, economic, and educational exchanges between the two cities."}, "D2S4": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 355, "end": 362, "text": "History"}, "D2S5": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 363, "end": 371, "text": "--------"}, "D2S6": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 373, "end": 557, "text": "The idea of twinning Rosh HaAyin and Evansville was first proposed in 2001 by a delegation of Israeli business leaders, who visited Evansville to explore potential trade opportunities."}, "D2S7": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 558, "end": 718, "text": "Following a series of meetings and discussions, the mayors of both cities signed a formal agreement on October 12, 2003, establishing the twinning relationship."}, "D2S8": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 719, "end": 726, "text": "Studies"}, "D2S9": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 727, "end": 735, "text": "--------"}, "D2S10": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 737, "end": 1081, "text": "A 2005 study published in the Journal of International Relations and Development found that the Rosh HaAyin-Evansville twinning had led to a significant increase in trade between the two cities, with Israeli exports to Evansville increasing by 25% and American exports to Rosh HaAyin increasing by 30% in the first two years of the partnership."}, "D2S11": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1082, "end": 1085, "text": "(1)"}, "D2S12": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1087, "end": 1350, "text": "A 2010 study conducted by the University of Evansville's Center for Economic Development found that the twinning had also led to an increase in cultural exchanges, with over 500 students and professionals participating in exchange programs between the two cities."}, "D2S13": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1351, "end": 1354, "text": "(2)"}, "D2S14": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1356, "end": 1362, "text": "Events"}, "D2S15": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1363, "end": 1371, "text": "--------"}, "D2S16": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1373, "end": 1467, "text": "The Rosh HaAyin-Evansville twinning has been marked by several high-profile events, including:"}, "D2S17": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1469, "end": 1606, "text": "* The 2004 Rosh HaAyin-Evansville Cultural Festival, which featured performances by Israeli and American musicians, dancers, and artists."}, "D2S18": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1607, "end": 1760, "text": "* The 2007 Evansville-Rosh HaAyin Business Forum, which brought together business leaders from both cities to discuss trade and investment opportunities."}, "D2S19": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1761, "end": 1903, "text": "* The 2012 Rosh HaAyin-Evansville Student Exchange Program, which saw 20 students from each city participate in a month-long exchange program."}, "D2S20": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1904, "end": 1914, "text": "References"}, "D2S21": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1915, "end": 1925, "text": "----------"}, "D2S22": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1927, "end": 2001, "text": "(1) \"The Impact of Sister City Relationships on International Trade\" by A."}, "D2S23": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2002, "end": 2014, "text": "Cohen and J."}, "D2S24": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2015, "end": 2078, "text": "Smith, Journal of International Relations and Development, Vol."}, "D2S25": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2079, "end": 2085, "text": "8, No."}, "D2S26": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2086, "end": 2094, "text": "2, 2005."}, "D2S27": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2095, "end": 2173, "text": "(2) \"The Rosh HaAyin-Evansville Twinning: A Study of Cultural Exchanges\" by J."}, "D2S28": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2174, "end": 2188, "text": "Johnson and M."}, "D2S29": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2189, "end": 2259, "text": "Davis, University of Evansville Center for Economic Development, 2010."}}, "original_cards": [], "current_answers": ["Osnabrück", "Rosh HaAyin"], "candidate_answers": [{"candidate_id": "R0", "answer": "Osnabrück", "origin": "initial"}, {"candidate_id": "R1", "answer": "Rosh HaAyin", "origin": "initial"}]}
